  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Ph2 Lebanon Crisis Response: Burj hammoud Drop in Centre to assist IDPs living on the streets in Beirut</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support at-risk displaced individuals in Beirut by ensuring dignified access to food and hygiene services. Specifically, Christian Aid (CA), in partnership with Mouvement Social (MSL), will provide vulnerable internally displaced persons (IDPs) with access to essential non-food items, including WASH/hygiene kits, washing machines, dryers, and hygiene supplies through a well-equipped drop-in centre located in the Burj Hammoud area. At this centre, MSL will also support 60 IDPs with training and resources to develop income-generating activities, based on priorities identified through community consultations.</narrative>
  </description>
